{%- comment -%}
MessagePack, on every generated contract.

NJsonSchema renders Class.Annotations into each class it writes and ships the template empty, so
overriding it adds attributes and changes nothing else about the generated code. The rest of the
DTO generator is untouched: a custom template directory overrides one file at a time and falls
back to the embedded template for every name it does not find.

Named mode: the member's key is the name the document publishes, pinned per member in
Class.Property.Annotations.liquid. keyAsPropertyName alone would write the C# member name, which
is NJsonSchema's PascalCasing of the wire name - agreeing with the server only for as long as two
unrelated PascalCase implementations agree.
{%- endcomment -%}
[MessagePack.MessagePackObject(true)]
